From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:43:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: follow the system's dark mode in web pages

Pages always saw a light system: prefers-color-scheme never matched
dark, and pages that support a dark color scheme stayed light. iOS had
no ui::OsSettingsProvider, so NativeTheme never learned the system's
appearance, and IOSContentBrowserClient never set the preferred color
scheme in the web preferences, which default to light.

Add OsSettingsProviderIOS, which reads the light or dark appearance of
the app's window scenes and notifies when it changes (trait change
registration on each window scene; scenes that connect later are
picked up when they activate). IOSContentBrowserClient now sets the
pages' preferred color scheme from NativeTheme, and asks for the web
preferences to be updated when it changes.

Status: verified at Chromium 4558926c in the iOS 27 simulator: with a
page that uses prefers-color-scheme and color-scheme: light dark,
switching the system appearance (simctl ui appearance) turns the page,
its media query, matchMedia listener and form controls dark and back
while it is open, and pages opened in dark mode load dark. google.com
stays light here, as it does in Safari on the same simulator (its own
dark theme setting).

